# **"eol=lf" and not "text=auto" alone, and that is a fix.**
#
# With "text=auto", git does store LF but leaves each machine to decide what
# it writes on disk. GitHub's Windows runners have "core.autocrlf=true", so
# they converted to CRLF on checkout, and the format gate, which follows the
# "end_of_line = lf" of .editorconfig, went red on the pipeline while it
# passed locally.
#
# "eol=lf" settles it for everyone, whatever the configuration of whoever
# clones.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
*.patch text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
